# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not and must never carry a value.
#
# Only ONE target needs a key: `make record`, which refreshes the model cassettes against the live
# Console API. Everything else - `make ci`, `make eval`, `make repro`, the whole test suite - runs in
# replay mode against committed cassettes, offline and free. CI deliberately has no key at all: if a
# change makes CI need one, that change has broken the reproducibility claim and the missing key is
# the symptom rather than the problem.
#
# `make record` reads `.env` (and only `make record` - every other target is offline in replay and
# has no business holding a credential). The shell always wins: a value already exported is never
# overwritten by this file, so a `.env` cannot silently shadow the account you meant to use.
#
# A key exported in your shell is still the safest option, because one that never touches the
# filesystem cannot be committed by accident. `.env` is the next best thing and is the one that
# survives a shell going away: it is gitignored, and `tools/guard/secret_guard.py` runs in
# `make ci` and fails the build on a credential in any tracked file.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxx
